IO-04: read bare-number [OPTIONS] times and steps as decimal hours

Legacy SWMM reads START_TIME, END_TIME, REPORT_START_TIME, WET_STEP,
DRY_STEP, REPORT_STEP and RULE_STEP with datetime_strToTime(), where a bare
number is decimal hours ("START_TIME 6.5" is 06:30, "REPORT_STEP 0.25" is
15 minutes). OptionsHandler read them with parse_time_seconds(), where a
bare number is seconds, so the same deck started at 00:00:06 and reported
every 0.25 s. A whole-token number is now taken as decimal hours, converted
as legacy does (h/24 days for a time of day; whole seconds for a step), and
anything else still goes to parse_time_seconds(). ROUTING_STEP,
MINIMUM_STEP and LENGTHENING_STEP stay in seconds, as in legacy. Clock
strings (HH:MM:SS) are read exactly as before.

Four unit tests (test_dw_unsteady_friction, test_dw_tpa, test_fv_tpa_closure,
test_fv_unsteady_friction) wrote REPORT_STEP as bare seconds (0.5, 1, 2, 5),
which EPA SWMM reads as hours; they now write the same steps as clock
strings (00:00:00.5, 00:00:01, ...), which mean the same to the unpatched
engine.

Requires: IO-02 (this patch edits the lines IO-02 adds its range checks to)

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after IO-02_swmm600.patch:
    git apply IO-04_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/OptionsHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/OptionsHandler.cpp
index 80b714e..2fc4e26 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/OptionsHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/OptionsHandler.cpp
@@ -86,6 +86,7 @@
 #include <charconv>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstring>
+#include <limits>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
@@ -100,6 +101,15 @@ static std::string norm(std::string_view sv) {
     return Tokenizer::to_upper(sv);
 }
 
+// Seconds in a clock time H:MM[:SS]. A token that is neither a number nor a
+// clock time gives NaN, which the range checks below reject (parse_time_seconds
+// alone would read it as 0).
+static double clock_seconds(std::string_view sv) {
+    if (sv.find(':') == std::string_view::npos)
+        return std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN();
+    return parse_time_seconds(sv);
+}
+
 // legacy findmatch / match (input.c): a keyword matches when it is a
 // case-insensitive PREFIX of the token — `STEADYFLOW` is STEADY, `DYNWAVE2`
 // DYNWAVE. `tok` is already upper-cased by norm().
@@ -278,21 +288,27 @@ void handle_options(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& line
